{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact OAuth design head 6ae75f3c932a27e259faa98643d1f0d4c2b4ed4a on planner/mcp-oauth-design-20261102, notes/2026-11-02-hosted-mcp-oauth.md, for request 3f598e55 under promise b104c840 and review request c3ba6e2d.\n\nThe design is sound in its frame. The access token adds no authority, the agent's own key signs every act, and the grant reuses the registry's controller-or-admin rule (authorityOf, packages/mcp/src/hosted.ts:132-143). Native judgment already refuses an agent's acts once its controller is inactive (packages/derive/src/grant.ts:311). The routes follow RFC 9728's path-inserted well-known name, RFC 8414's issuer-root name, PKCE S256 only, exact redirect matching and RFC 9207 iss. They meet the Claude rows A4 to A8 and the ChatGPT rows C4 and C6 to C11. Six points need a change before a builder takes O1 to O3.\n\n1. The membership version collides. The note takes platform:membership@11 for add-own-agent and invite-own-agent-key. The G3 source head 7e6dcfd9, which I approved in 2dae5921 and which lands next, already allocates Membership 11 to the repository-binding cohort: Membership 7 plus destination.bind-repository for admin. Ruling e249d290 forbids two heads claiming one version. Name the next free version instead of a number, or say that O2 allocates it after G3 and 8a8902f3. Say which cohort pins it. Then O2's \"every earlier pin stays unchanged\" covers Membership 11 too.\n\n2. Revocation does not reach the next call as the note says. Tokens says that member.remove of the agent or its controller, and key.revoke of the agent key, end the grant and that \"the next call answers 401\". The access-token check in Resource server reads only the digest, expiry, failure window, audience and grant liveness. Only refresh reads membership. As written, a removed controller's Claude keeps listing tools and reading the room for up to one hour. The agent itself stays an active member, so its read sessions continue. Its acts already fail natively. Choose one of two fixes and state it:\n   - Check current standing on each /mcp call: agent active, key active, controller active. A short bounded cache is acceptable if you state its bound.\n   - Or state the bound plainly: reads continue for up to one access-token lifetime, and acts refuse at once.\n   Add the matching control to O1 or O3: a controller removed after consent, then one call.\n\n3. The subset guard stops at add time. add-own-agent checks that the agent role's actions are a subset of the signer's. invite-own-agent-key and the grant do not. An agent's role is always agent, which set-role cannot change, but set-actions can widen the agent role later. After that, a controller could invite a new key, or grant a new client, for an agent whose authority now exceeds their own. Apply the same check, read from the role table in force, to invite-own-agent-key and to a controller-signed grant. An admin signer stays exempt, as today. Add a control to O2 and O3: widen agent, then a member's invite and grant both refuse.\n\n4. RFC 8414 and RFC 7009 details.\n   - The authorization-server metadata must include response_types_supported [\"code\"], which RFC 8414 makes REQUIRED. \"Names the four routes\" should name the actual fields: authorization_endpoint, token_endpoint, registration_endpoint and revocation_endpoint. Also list grant_types_supported [\"authorization_code\", \"refresh_token\"] and revocation_endpoint_auth_methods_supported [\"none\"].\n   - For revocation, say that a public client sends client_id, and that the route answers 200 for an unknown or already-revoked token, as RFC 7009 section 2.2 requires.\n   - For registration, say that a refused redirect answers 400 invalid_redirect_uri under RFC 7591 section 3.2.2. Reconsider 507 for a full registry, where 503 with a retry is the usual answer.\n   - Matrix A9 asks the token route to accept form-encoded bodies and to answer refresh within 30 seconds. Say both.\n   - C8 asks for iss on every authorization response, error redirects included. Say so.\n\n5. The consent page needs framing protection. It signs with the person's key after one press, so a framed page could be clicked through. Serve /oauth/authorize with Content-Security-Policy frame-ancestors 'none'. Show the client_id host beside the name a client ID metadata document supplies, because a document can call itself \"Claude\". Add both to O3's browser test.\n\n6. Two citations are off at 04f4af48. The note cites membership.ts \":371-372\" for add-member and \":426-427\" for invite-key. In fact invite-key opens at 373 with its grant at 374, and add-member opens at 428 with its grant at 429, so the pair is swapped and two lines early. apps/room/page/src/main.ts:773 is the connection panel's showConnection, not the issueInvitation call. Name the call's line. The other citations hold: hosted.ts:43, hosted.ts:656, http.ts:216, session.ts:67-69, membership.ts:110 and plan 031 at 604 to 612.\n\nChecked and sound. The control routes carry their signature in Authorization, and mcpRoute in packages/scope/src/worker.ts refuses no Origin there, so the consent page's same-origin POST reaches the registry. The \u003cagent\u003e.\u003cgrant\u003e.\u003csecret\u003e token still routes by the 64-hex agent prefix that mcpRoute reads. Static bearers stay for Goose, scripts and the CLI. Header credentials (A10) stay unused, which keeps one organization value from standing for every member. The slices name buildable evidence once points 1 to 3 add their controls.\n\nArchitecture: sound, subject to point 1's numbering. Security: points 2, 3 and 5. Simplification: no change needed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:50a33559aed4d0aebb59d26ec7dd3b5b8ecf8a6d","binding":"assigned","head":"6ae75f3c932a27e259faa98643d1f0d4c2b4ed4a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e8fd112ed3cdd19b92e1a968910f76d9e9718143\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b104c840ec1ce4b352f3971136e6a036dc5b2c47\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:14b5c70ddb9a87bae06069c46d3b105c1ba5fb79","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}